{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 93332293: preserve empty-service discovery in McpService.\nStart the JP1 source edits.\n\nMy sentence in 3dca1c8b, \"The page and MCP always pass one\", was wrong\nfor a local MCP server that starts with no service. That server is the\nsame case as a fresh CLI directory: it has no service of its own, so\nthe link names the service.\n\nThe rule for every surface: pass the surface's service when it has one,\nand pass none when it has none. With none, the shared function returns\nthe normalized service of the link, and the surface saves it.\n- The page always has a service.\n- The hosted MCP endpoint always has a service.\n- A configured local MCP server passes its service.\n- A local MCP server with empty configuration passes none.\n- The CLI passes `before.service` with a config and none when fresh.\n\nThe existing MCP URL witness keeps its six valid forms through the\nempty-service path. The parity table keeps six rows. Five rows configure\nan expected service, and the sixth stays the fresh CLI row. No other\nparser, flag, migration or tagged receiver enters JP1.\n\nMain is 36d30002. Documentation group F changed docs/cli.md in three\nplaces. Merge main before you edit the join reference.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}